    <ferc:GeneralInformationAboutStatesInWhichRespondentServicesWereRendered id="f-75" contextRef="c-51">The California Independent System Operator Corporation assumed control over Citizens S-Line Transmission LLC's transmission assets/entitlements and uses those assets to provide transmission service to utilities within the State of California.</ferc:GeneralInformationAboutStatesInWhichRespondentServicesWereRendered>
    <ferc:AuthorityByWhichTheReceivershipOrTrusteeshipWasCreated id="f-77" contextRef="c-51" xsi:nil="true" />
    <ferc:NameOfReceiverOrTrusteeHoldingPropertyOfTheRespondent id="f-78" contextRef="c-51" xsi:nil="true" />
    <ferc:ControlOverRespondentTextBlock id="f-80" contextRef="c-51">&lt;p&gt;Citizens S-Line Transmission LLC (&amp;quot;the Company&amp;quot;) is a limited liability company, organized under the laws of the Delaware Limited Liability Company Act. The Company is a 100% subsidiary of Citizens Enterprises Corporation. Thus, Citizens Enterprises Corporation indirectly manages and controls the Company.&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:ControlOverRespondentTextBlock>
